# The McDonnell Douglas F-15C Eagle, two F100-PW-220s: JSBSim's f15 made to fly
# to the USAF's Standard Aircraft Characteristics (assets/figures/f15c.xml) by
# tools/make_f15c.py.
#
#   name TEXT...                 what it is called
#   model NAME                   its JSBSim model, in data/jsbsim/aircraft
#   start AIRSPEED_KT THROTTLE   a flight begun in the air: its calibrated
#                                airspeed, and the throttle that holds it
#
# Its published figures, if it has them, are data/figures/MODEL.xml, and its
# selftest's log data/selftest/MODEL.log (src/sim/catalogue.hpp).

name McDonnell Douglas F-15C Eagle
model f15c
class fighter
start 300 0.49
# The speedbrake lever works its speedbrake (src/sim/catalogue.hpp).
speedbrakes
# Her main tyres and brakes, for a wet runway's grip (docs/ASSETS.md):
# UFC 3-260-02 (draft, Oct 2014) table 4-1a: the F-15's 34.5x9.75-18 main at
# 305 psi, at 81,000 lb (an F-15E's weight - the C's is not given apart);
# Hydro-Aire's Mark III, continuously modulating (Crane's brake control
# overview).
brakes 305 fully-modulating
